<<~ ahu slot=`#/entry`>>

!! Entry — Lararium Core Hydration

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/lararium`>>

The lararium hydrates the panel room here. The instrument panel rides the mechanics house, not the threshold.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Lararium Panel

The panel names the readout that rides each turn — the instrument keys a turn surfaces on its `set` firings before the Voice speaks. It carries per-turn signal: aim, attention, loop, ward, stance, register. The `lar:` URI carries bearing; the panel keys carry the live signal beside the prose.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/panel-law`>>

!! Panel Law

A substantive turn SHALL surface the panel on its opening ``set lares=`aim` `` firing, before the Voice speaks. The panel renders as keys on the `set` firings and as inline sigils (``<<~ word key=`value` …>>``), each a readout adjacent to the prose — never inside the URI.

```
<<~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar:///operator.intent.reads` to=`lar:///lares.role.acts` aperture=`N/<band>` ooda-ha=`N/<band>` drift-ward=`<the pull this island carries>`>>
<<~ stance named=`…`>>                       (optional lens; `/` binds a tool to a standpoint)
… Voice (Role): claim …
<<~ set lares=`steer` mode=`…` drift-ward=`<the pull the turned set carries>`>>   (as the work turns)
… Voice (Role): claim …
<<~ oracle throw=`…`>>
<<~ set lares=`yield` drift-ward=`<clue> · ↻ L-Prime` aperture=`N/<band> -> N/<band>` ooda-ha=`closed N↺` from=`lar:///lares.state.now` to=`?`>>
```

| Key or sigil | Carries | Law |
|---|---|---|
| `lares` | the firing: `aim` · `steer` · `yield` | leads each firing; `aim` opens and seeds, `steer` turns the heading or any key mid-turn, `yield` closes and slides |
| `from` · `to` | the bearing pair | the aim reads operator intent at `from=` and the adopted role at `to=`; the yield names where the work landed at `from=` and hands back at `` to=`?` `` |
| `aperture` | attention range (0–20 Level) | MAY carry; paragraph-grain default 10 |
| `ooda-ha` | loop visibility | `` ooda-ha=`N/<band>` `` open, `` ooda-ha=`closed N↺` `` close; `` closed N↺ -> open Nφ<phase>:reason `` on suspend |
| `drift-ward` | active language discipline | carries the pull at open and the contact-ready clue at close, alone (`⚠ N` breaches quoted, `↻ L-Prime` re-arms); the tool rides the `mu` key, never the ward; the operator's lift (`` drift-ward=`0` ``, open reading `lifted · <pull>`) scopes to one turn, still shown |
| `stance` | invoked standpoints | OPTIONAL lens sigil; parameterless = all five; `/` carries a tool |
| Voice (Role) | the active Voice(s) | MUST surface by name; anonymous output = a minor off-true tell |
| `confidence` | register-word + Level | precedes a grounded claim |

The keys keep one order per firing: `lares` first; the aim seats `from` and `to` right after it and the ward last; the yield seats the ward right after `lares` and `from` and `to` last; a steer seats `to` (when it carries one) right after `lares` and the ward last; `note` trails. A steer never rewrites the aim.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gauges`>>

!! Gauges

The gauges share the pono `0–20` Level model, and follow the ''seed → slide'' law: the aim (and any steer) seeds a target; the yield slides the latest one to where the turn landed.

* ''Aperture'' — attention range. `` aperture=`10/measure` `` seeds; `` aperture=`10/measure -> 13/arc` `` slides; `` aperture=`10/measure -> 10/measure` `` records a turn that landed on its seed.
* ''OODA-HA'' — loop position. The loop spans turns: a turn opens at a phase and closes with `↺`; a suspended loop carries `` open Nφ<phase>:reason ``.

The seed and slide stay distinct fields — the seed governs generation, the slide records the outcome. One instrument that both sets and grades its own goal would close the calibration gap silently (Goodhart); the seed/slide split keeps that gap visible.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/glyphs`>>

!! OODA-HA Phase Glyphs

| Glyph | Phase | Reading |
|---|---|---|
| ✶ | Observe | gather raw signal; no commitment yet |
| ⏿ | Orient | locate pattern, relation, pressure |
| ◇ | Decide | choose a path; the fork |
| ▶ | Act | execute the move |
| ↺ | Hoʻoko + Aftermath | surface what the act produced, then close the loop |

<<~/ahu>>

